        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Battle of Plataea</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Date</span><span class="info-stat-val">August 479 BCE; Paul A. Rahe and Theodore Cuyler Young Jr. estimate 27 August, Rahe allowing the 27th or 28th</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Place</span><span class="info-stat-val">Near the city of Plataea in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boeotia">Boeotia</a>, central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a>, on and around the Asopos river; the Persian camp stood on its north bank</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">The two sides</span><span class="info-stat-val">The Hellenic alliance led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sparta">Sparta</a>, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/athens">Athens</a>, Corinth, Tegea, Megara and other <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/city-state">city-states</a>, under the Spartan regent <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pausanias-general">Pausanias</a>, with 78,000 soldiers by Konecny's estimate; an Achaemenid army under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mardonius">Mardonius</a>, allied with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boeotia">Boeotia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thessaly">Thessaly</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-macedon">Macedon</a>, with 70,000 by Lazenby's estimate and 120,000 by Connolly's</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Outcome</span><span class="info-stat-val">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greeks">Greeks</a> routed the Persian infantry and killed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mardonius">Mardonius</a>, then stormed the Persian camp. The second Persian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-persian-invasion-of-greece">invasion of Greece</a> ended.</span></div>
