    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>Figures for both armies rest on estimates. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herodotus">Herodotus</a> gives the Spartan contribution as 45,000 men, and modern estimates of the Persian army run from 40,000 to 120,000, mostly from the size of its camp.</li><li>The Greek retreat on the night before the battle went wrong, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mardonius">Mardonius</a>, thinking the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greeks">Greeks</a> were in full retreat, ordered a pursuit that brought on the fighting.</li><li><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herodotus">Herodotus</a> gives 652 Greek dead, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/plutarch">Plutarch</a> 1,360 and Diodorus 10,000, and says only 3,000 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persians">Persians</a> survived the fighting at the camp.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herodotus">Herodotus</a> says the Spartans sent 45,000 men, of whom 5,000 were <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spartiates">Spartiates</a> and 35,000 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/helots">helots</a>, seven helots for each Spartiate, and one tenth of the Persian loot went to the regent <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pausanias-general">Pausanias</a>, not to the state of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sparta">Sparta</a>.</p></aside>
    </section>

